[
{ type: install
  message: <<EOM
REVYTECHCommander is installed. Before enabling services:

  1. mkdir -p ${PREFIX}/etc/cloudbsd/revytechcommander
     cp ${PREFIX}/etc/cloudbsd/revytechcommander/config.json.sample \
        ${PREFIX}/etc/cloudbsd/revytechcommander/config.json
  2. Fill PLACEHOLDERS: public domain, bcrypt password_hash, provider
     API keys, FreeGrok base_url, Postgres DSN, NATS URL, Caddy DNS-01
     token. Secrets may also be supplied via REVYTECH_* environment
     variables (see README).
  3. pw groupadd revytech
     pw useradd revytech -g revytech -s /usr/sbin/nologin \
        -d /var/db/revytechcommander -m
     chmod 0600 ${PREFIX}/etc/cloudbsd/revytechcommander/config.json
     chown revytech:revytech ${PREFIX}/etc/cloudbsd/revytechcommander/config.json
  4. Apply ${DATADIR}/deploy/sql/001_init.sql.
  5. Point Caddy at ${DATADIR}/deploy/Caddyfile. The gateway must NOT bind
     public 443.

Single-node (meta service starts conductor, worker, gateway in order):

     sysrc revytechcommander_enable=YES
     sysrc revytechcommander_gateway_enable=NO \
           revytechcommander_worker_enable=NO \
           revytechcommander_conductor_enable=NO
     service revytechcommander start

Do not also enable the per-role scripts when the meta service is on
(double-start). Nomad-managed hosts must leave every *_enable at NO.

Config is JSON only. Validate with:
  revytechcommander --check-config -config ${PREFIX}/etc/cloudbsd/revytechcommander/config.json

The binary is one file with subcommands:
  revytechcommander gateway|worker|conductor

Sample rc.conf keys: ${DATADIR}/deploy/rc.conf.sample
Nomad/Consul/WireGuard/NATS: ${DATADIR}/deploy
EOM
}
]
